        <mxCell id="note" value="" style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#E0E3E7;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="680" width="780" height="270" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notetitle" value="Tasks (you build it — answer key at bottom of NOTES.md)" style="text;html=1;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1A2027;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="78" y="692" width="600" height="22" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notebody" value="1.  Bring up eBGP to both ISPs + iBGP r1↔r2 + next-hop-self; originate 192.0.2.0/24. See TWO paths to 8.8.8.0/24.&#10;2.  OUTBOUND TE — Local Preference (route-map in on r1): make all egress exit via ISP-A. Rule 2 beats rule 7.&#10;3.  INBOUND TE — AS-path prepend (out on r2): make the internet prefer ISP-A for 192.0.2.0/24. (MED only same-AS.)&#10;4.  Communities — tag routes, drive local-pref from a tag; send-community.&#10;5.  Don't be transit — prefix-list/route-map out so you advertise ONLY 192.0.2.0/24 to the ISPs.&#10;&#10;Best-path order: Weight ▸ Local-Pref ▸ Originated ▸ AS-path ▸ Origin ▸ MED ▸ eBGP&gt;iBGP ▸ IGP metric ▸ router-id." style="text;html=1;fontSize=11;align=left;fontColor=#3C4A5A;spacingLeft=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="78" y="716" width="744" height="220" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
